MULTI-AGENT PATTERN: SPECIALIST AGENT ENSEMBLES — Complete Consolidation
The Core Concept
Instead of one generalist agent making decisions, bring in multiple specialist agents analyzing the same input in parallel, then synthesize their insights into a single coherent recommendation.
--------------------------------
PART 1: THE PROBLEM & SOLUTION
--------------------------------
The Problem: Generalist Agents Are Limited
A single generalist agent:

❌ Lacks deep expertise in specific domains
❌ Makes incomplete decisions
❌ Misses critical risks
❌ Can't balance competing priorities
Real Example: A business expansion decision needs:

Financial analysis (revenue potential, profitability)
Risk assessment (competitive threats, regulatory risks)
Compliance review (policy alignment, legal requirements)
A single agent can't do all three well.

The Solution: Specialist Ensembles
Bring in three domain experts analyzing in parallel:

