--------------------------------
PART 10: KEY ADVANTAGES
--------------------------------
✅ Better Decisions — Multiple perspectives catch what single agents miss
✅ Parallel Execution — Faster than sequential (3 agents in parallel time)
✅ Risk Mitigation — Different specialists identify different risks
✅ Confidence Levels — Know how confident each specialist is
✅ Transparency — See reasoning from each specialist
✅ Scalability — Add more specialists as needed
✅ Robustness — If one specialist fails, others continue

--------------------------------
PART 11: WHEN TO USE
--------------------------------
✅ Use When:

Decision has multiple dimensions (financial, risk, compliance)
Need high-quality decisions
Have time for parallel analysis
Want to reduce decision risk
Need transparency and explainability
❌ Don't Use When:

Need instant decisions
Simple, single-dimension problems
Cost is critical constraint
Real-time requirements
PART 12: KEY TAKEAWAYS
✅ Specialist Agents — Each focuses on one domain
✅ Parallel Execution — All specialists run simultaneously
✅ Flow State Variables — Shared context between stages
✅ Orchestrator — Synthesizes insights and identifies trade-offs
✅ Decision Agent — Makes final recommendation with confidence
✅ Higher Quality — 0.88 quality vs 0.65 for single agent
✅ Transparency — See reasoning from each specialist
✅ Scalability — Add specialists as needed

